<title>MEXICO: Mexico suspends Pulsar lumber project - paper.</title>
<headline>Mexico suspends Pulsar lumber project - paper.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican authorities have suspended a massive lumber project of  Grupo Pulsar because the Monterrey-based company is not complying with environmental requirements, daily Reforma reported Monday.</p>
<p>Citing authorities in the southern state of Tabasco, Reforma said the project, which started in 1994 and has seen investment of $10 million in the planting of 1,000 hectares of eucalyptus, lacks required environmental impact studies.</p>
<p>Pulsar aims to expand the lumber project into other southern states such as Chiapas and Campeche, investing a further $30 million, Reforma said.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530</p>
